---
title: "API Versioning"
description: "Learn how to select a date-based version for supported Datadog API operations."
---

Datadog API operations use their default behavior unless you select a date-based API version. Operations that support date-based versions include an **API version** selector in the API reference.

To request a dated version directly, send its date in the `DD-API-Version` header:

```bash
DD-API-Version: YYYY-MM-DD
```

The version selector updates the request and response schemas, cURL command, and client library examples together. Schema fields that changed from the preceding version are marked as added or removed.

You can also link to a selected operation version. The API reference stores the selection in the `datadog-api-version` query parameter, using the format `v1-YYYY-MM-DD`.

See the [API changelog][1] for changes associated with each version.

[1]: /api/changelog/
